WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.214 --> 00:00:07.010
DONNA SCHUT: Hi, everyone.

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:09.350
Hope you're safe and doing well.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:12.320
Thank you for joining this
session on Google Cloud's AI

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.300
Adoption Framework.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.680
AI is increasingly
the new frontier

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:19.560
in digital transformation
and is well positioned

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:24.010
to drive value across all
aspects of an organization.

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:25.590
We believe that the
enterprises that

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:29.010
invest in building custom
AI and industry solutions

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:31.890
are better positioned to be
the global economic leaders

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.580
of tomorrow.

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:36.730
As McKinsey's paper
"Modeling the Impact of AI

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:41.200
on the World Economy" indicated,
companies that fully absorb AI

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:43.760
could double their cash flow.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:45.550
We will be presenting
on a framework aimed

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:48.790
at enabling organizations
to build an effective AI

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:52.900
capability informed by
Google's own evolution in AI

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:54.730
as well as many
years of experience

00:00:54.730 --> 00:00:58.240
in helping cloud customers
solve complex challenges

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:02.270
from startups to enterprises
in various industries.

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:05.170
So if you're looking to help
your organization leverage

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:08.348
AI successfully, whether
at the start or far

00:01:08.348 --> 00:01:10.390
along your journey, you
are in the right session.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.240
As you may have
seen, we recently

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:17.400
published a white
paper on this which

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:19.770
Khalid and I wrote with
the help of many experts

00:01:19.770 --> 00:01:21.510
from across Google.

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:25.890
Our coauthors Barbara,
Finn, Valentine, Lak,

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:29.130
and us are available to
answer your questions

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:30.930
during this week.

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:33.060
To briefly introduce
ourselves, I'm

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:35.310
Donna, the technical
account manager

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:38.340
defining strategic roadmaps with
our advanced machine-learning

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:41.040
customers and
overseeing the delivery

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.613
of large-scale,
cutting-edge projects.

00:01:44.613 --> 00:01:47.030
KHALID SALAMA: And I'm Khalid,
a cloud solutions architect

00:01:47.030 --> 00:01:48.560
focusing on designing
and building

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:50.360
machine-learning
systems in Google Cloud.

00:01:53.673 --> 00:01:55.840
DONNA SCHUT: Before going
into the framework itself,

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:59.500
I wanted to share why I'm
so passionate about this.

00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:02.420
I used to play chess at
an international level,

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:04.690
and this sparked
my interest in AI.

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:08.169
It showed me how AI can push
the boundaries of our thinking

00:02:08.169 --> 00:02:10.360
and accelerate our learning.

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:12.970
A good example of
this is AlphaZero,

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:14.710
a machine-learning
system developed

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:17.410
by DeepMind that plays chess.

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:19.180
This gave a new
perspective on how

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:21.450
to effectively play the game.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:23.650
And in a similar
way, AI can give us

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:27.220
a new perspective on how to
solve business challenges.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:28.960
More than ever, I
think it's important

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:32.500
that we leverage AI to tackle
the big societal problems

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:35.230
like health and sustainability.

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:38.890
While the value of AI is clear,
building an AI capability

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:40.720
presents challenges.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:43.150
Customers often seek
our advice on how

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:45.220
they can leverage machine
learning effectively

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:47.080
to gain business value.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:50.290
They ask us questions like,
what role should we hire?

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:52.480
and how should we
structure our teams?

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.760
As you move from creating
models to putting them

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:58.690
into production, different
skill sets are required.

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:02.500
And how can we make data
discoverable, shareable,

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:03.820
and reusable?

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:06.340
One of the key
blockers of AI adoption

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:08.650
is the lack of high-quality
data and making

00:03:08.650 --> 00:03:11.590
it accessible in a secure way.

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:15.220
On top of that, they ask us,
how can we deploy and operate

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:18.700
machine-learning models
in production at scale?

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:22.900
Customers aspire to run powerful
algorithms on large data sets

00:03:22.900 --> 00:03:25.790
while controlling cost.

00:03:25.790 --> 00:03:28.190
Building an AI
capability encompasses

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:31.820
many different aspects, and
focusing on just one aspect,

00:03:31.820 --> 00:03:35.300
like the technology and not the
people needed to implement it,

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:39.180
can result in wasted
resources and no impact.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:42.960
That's why it's so important
to have a clear roadmap.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.580
Working with
customers, we wanted

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:46.980
to help them be
successful no matter where

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:50.280
they are in their journey,
so a year ago we envisioned

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:52.350
a framework to
enable organizations

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:55.140
to leverage machine
learning effectively

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:57.270
and gain business value.

00:03:57.270 --> 00:04:00.390
Chess is about creating a
vision and defining the steps

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:01.620
to get there.

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:05.220
We applied the same structure
to building AI capabilities

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:08.212
and conceived the AI
Adoption Framework.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:13.290
Google Cloud's AI
Adoption Framework

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:15.540
is essentially a guide
for organizations

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:18.899
who want to build an
effective AI capability.

00:04:18.899 --> 00:04:21.060
The framework covers
the questions customers

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:24.690
have asked us in the
areas of the technology

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:28.350
to develop platforms and
solutions, the people who

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:31.230
will implement and
manage that technology,

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:34.110
the data that fuels
that technology,

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:38.030
and the processes that
govern the whole of it.

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:42.110
Success requires an integrated
lens between these areas.

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:44.540
The interplay between
these four areas

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:46.820
gives rise to six themes--

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:53.690
learn, lead, access,
secure, scale, and automate.

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:55.920
Based on our experience
with customers,

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:57.770
these are the six
themes you need

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.690
to address to be successful.

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:06.030
To briefly introduce
each theme--

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:09.840
learn is the interplay
between people and technology.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:12.810
It entails hiring talent,
upskilling your staff

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:14.790
through learning
programs, and working

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:18.310
with experienced partners.

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:21.430
Lead is the interplay
between people and process.

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:24.340
It refers to leaders
sponsoring AI initiatives

00:05:24.340 --> 00:05:28.910
and how teams are structured
and collaborate with each other.

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:32.100
Access is the interplay
between people and data.

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:33.890
It's about data
management and making

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:37.100
data assets and machine-learning
artifacts discoverable,

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:40.430
shareable, and reusable.

00:05:40.430 --> 00:05:43.730
Secure is the interplay
between data and process.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:45.980
It addresses how you
classify and protect

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:49.820
data, build their systems,
and implement responsible AI

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:52.330
practices.

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:55.660
Scale is the interplay
between data and technology.

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.750
It covers how you use
cloud-native services to scale

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:01.330
with big data sets and
a large number of jobs

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:03.670
without operational overhead.

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:06.160
And lastly, automate
is the interplay

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:08.410
between technology and process.

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:10.630
It encompasses
deploying, executing,

00:06:10.630 --> 00:06:13.420
and operating technology for
machine-learning pipelines

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:18.950
in production efficiently,
frequently, and reliably.

00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:22.640
Your readiness is determined by
your current business practices

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:26.450
in each of the six themes
across three phases--

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:30.910
tactical, strategic,
and transformational.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:33.040
In the tactical
phase, the focus is

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:37.060
on easy adoption, minimal
disruption, and quick wins.

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:39.730
Different teams experiment
with simple analytics

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:43.120
use cases and benefit from
improved actionable insights

00:06:43.120 --> 00:06:44.480
from data--

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:46.480
for example, using
basic descriptive

00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:49.690
analytics to create a
customer-segmentation model.

00:06:49.690 --> 00:06:53.780
Complex problems are
outsourced to partners.

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:56.240
In the strategic
phase, AI is used

00:06:56.240 --> 00:07:00.320
to deliver sustainable business
value for your organization.

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:02.730
You typically form
a centralized team,

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:05.120
ensuring coordination,
consistent standards,

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:06.470
and governance.

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:09.020
A broader vision
steers AI adoption,

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:11.180
and your organization has
several machine-learning

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:14.420
systems deployed and maintained
in production, like propensity

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:18.390
modeling, demand forecasting,
and recommendations,

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:22.790
leveraging data sets from an
enterprise data warehouse.

00:07:22.790 --> 00:07:24.920
In the transformational
phase, AI

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:27.620
plays a key role in
the organization,

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:30.470
stimulating innovation
and supporting agility

00:07:30.470 --> 00:07:33.330
to create state of
the art algorithms--

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:35.240
for example, using
the language model

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:38.060
BERT to extract information
and answer questions

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:40.450
from COVID research papers.

00:07:40.450 --> 00:07:43.430
You cultivate a culture where
experimentation and learning

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:45.590
is continuous and encouraged.

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:47.780
Machine-learning
expertise has diffused

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:49.820
across the lines of
business, and there's

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:52.520
a mechanism in place for
scaling and promoting

00:07:52.520 --> 00:07:56.300
machine-learning capabilities
across the organization.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:59.810
All teams are empowered through
a platform that enables access

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:04.010
to useful data sets, prepared
features, reusable components,

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:06.490
and trained models.

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:09.190
When you overlay
the six themes--

00:08:09.190 --> 00:08:13.480
learn, lead, access, secure,
scale, and automate--

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:14.950
and the three phases--

00:08:14.950 --> 00:08:17.860
tactical, strategic,
and transformational--

00:08:17.860 --> 00:08:20.440
you get the AI Maturity Scale.

00:08:20.440 --> 00:08:24.100
You can use the AI Maturity
Scale to assess where you are

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:26.170
and define where you want to go.

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:28.810
The goal isn't necessarily
to become transformational

00:08:28.810 --> 00:08:32.900
in every aspect but to get
value every step of the way.

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:35.559
Now I'll hand over to
Khalid who will dive deeper

00:08:35.559 --> 00:08:39.440
into the Maturity
Scale for each theme.

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:41.179
KHALID SALAMA: Thank you, Donna.

00:08:41.179 --> 00:08:43.520
So the first theme
to discuss is learn.

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:45.530
As Donna mentioned,
it concerns aspects

00:08:45.530 --> 00:08:51.040
like upskilling, hiring, and
collaboration with partners.

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:52.690
In the tactical
phase, we've seen

00:08:52.690 --> 00:08:55.300
that learning about data
science and machine learning

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:58.120
is usually isolated
and self-motivated.

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:01.090
Your organization tends to
turn to third-party consultants

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:03.730
when facing compelling
machine-learning use cases

00:09:03.730 --> 00:09:06.760
rather than hiring to fill
the gaps in the skill set.

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:12.390
As your organization starts to
build a greater AI capability

00:09:12.390 --> 00:09:14.970
in-house, you hire
the required skills

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:17.100
for data science and
machine learning.

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:19.290
Typically, organizations
start to hire

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:22.500
machine-learning engineers in
addition to data scientists

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:26.800
to be able to productionize
their machine-learning models.

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:29.400
You also develop clear learning
[INAUDIBLE] with certification

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:31.140
to upskill your stuff.

00:09:31.140 --> 00:09:33.780
For example, using our
Google Cloud training

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:36.635
and certification programs.

00:09:36.635 --> 00:09:39.010
We've recently launched the
Professional Machine Learning

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:41.695
Engineer Certification to
assess your team's ability

00:09:41.695 --> 00:09:43.570
to design and build a
machine-learning system

00:09:43.570 --> 00:09:45.410
in Google Cloud.

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:47.200
Platform a partnership
perspective,

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:49.750
your organization chooses
a strategic partner

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:54.020
to provide specialized knowledge
in specific AI use cases.

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:56.920
For example, automating
document processing

00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:58.480
or building conversational apps.

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:03.750
Moving to the
transformational phase,

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:07.450
we've seen customers encouraging
P2P and community learning,

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:10.590
creating internal
knowledge bases and wikis,

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:13.450
and allowing staff rotations
across business functions

00:10:13.450 --> 00:10:17.580
to ensure tighter collaboration
and exchange of experience.

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:20.430
Your organization
now aims at hiring

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:23.810
AI and machine-learning
talent with industry expertise

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:27.640
to lead research and
innovation efforts.

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:30.100
Now let's move to
the lead theme which

00:10:30.100 --> 00:10:32.830
concerns with
business-leadership support

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:35.900
and team structure
and collaboration.

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:37.790
In the early phase
of the maturity,

00:10:37.790 --> 00:10:40.460
AI adoption is driven by
individual contributors

00:10:40.460 --> 00:10:42.920
with little or no
executive sponsorship.

00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:45.290
Thus the machine
learning initiatives

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:48.290
might not have a clear alignment
with your organization's

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:50.100
strategic goals.

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:52.520
The key step is to start with
your organization business

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:55.130
strategy and
priority to identify

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:57.020
the right
machine-learning use cases

00:10:57.020 --> 00:10:58.950
and pursue executive
sponsorship.

00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:04.990
As your senior executives
realize the importance of AI

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:07.270
for creating
competitive advantage,

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:09.400
they support and
fund AI projects

00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:12.500
to deliver value for
various business functions.

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:15.460
Now you can establish a
centralized cross-functional

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:18.310
advanced analytics team to
standardize the practices

00:11:18.310 --> 00:11:23.110
and guidelines and to
achieve strategic AI agenda.

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:24.640
This advanced
analytics team works

00:11:24.640 --> 00:11:27.310
on delivering prioritized
machine-learning projects

00:11:27.310 --> 00:11:30.453
and proactively clarifying
how AI can effectively

00:11:30.453 --> 00:11:31.620
address different use cases.

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:38.320
In the transformational
phase, each functional team

00:11:38.320 --> 00:11:41.440
has its own data scientists
with the right domain-specific

00:11:41.440 --> 00:11:43.780
expertise.

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:45.850
Having a centralized
machine-learning engineering

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:48.610
team and embedding that
scientists in the business

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:52.120
functions ensures both
strong technical standards

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:54.840
and effective business aligns.

00:11:54.840 --> 00:11:57.630
As AI shows to be
impactful to your business,

00:11:57.630 --> 00:11:59.310
the C-level executives
continuously

00:11:59.310 --> 00:12:03.630
demonstrate active sponsor
for innovative AI products.

00:12:03.630 --> 00:12:05.790
Such research and
innovation projects

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:08.640
aim at solving cutting-edge
business problems

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:11.100
and establishing the
organization name as a market

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:13.420
leader.

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:15.000
The third theme in
our framework is

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:18.090
access, which concerns
effective data management

00:12:18.090 --> 00:12:20.230
to enable shareability,
discoverability,

00:12:20.230 --> 00:12:22.930
and reuseablity.

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:24.940
In the early stages,
each team usually

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:27.670
manages its own data island
and machine-learning assets

00:12:27.670 --> 00:12:30.880
with no sharing
among other teams.

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:33.280
As a tactical step to
update your strategy,

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:36.130
you can look into building
a data lake containing

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:38.170
their own structured
and unstructured data

00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:41.170
feeds from across your
disparate systems.

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:44.200
This can form the foundation
for collecting, curating,

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:46.750
and sharing data across
your organization

00:12:46.750 --> 00:12:48.520
and creating managed
information objects.

00:12:52.940 --> 00:12:56.630
As your organization recognizes
data as a vital enterprise

00:12:56.630 --> 00:13:00.530
asset that fuels AI, you invest
in building an enterprise data

00:13:00.530 --> 00:13:03.770
warehouse which provides
an integrated information

00:13:03.770 --> 00:13:06.680
store and a unified data
model for different business

00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:09.140
functions.

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:12.240
The data warehouse empowers
data analysts, data scientists,

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:14.680
and data engineers
to perform their data

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:18.710
wrangling, exploration,
and analytics activities.

00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:20.920
For example, we work
with a media customer

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:25.330
that successfully uses BigQuery
as their enterprisewide data

00:13:25.330 --> 00:13:26.480
warehouse.

00:13:26.480 --> 00:13:29.380
This enabled their various teams
to perform analytical queries

00:13:29.380 --> 00:13:31.870
and information retrieval
from a centralized location.

00:13:35.550 --> 00:13:37.560
Besides, you start
to put together

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:40.070
a centralized repository
for machine-learning assets

00:13:40.070 --> 00:13:42.120
like notebooks
and code templates

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:45.160
and develop tools for
annotating and categorizing

00:13:45.160 --> 00:13:47.070
deficits and other
assets to enable

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:49.740
discoverability and usability.

00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:51.960
Data quality management
at this stage

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:54.840
is a business variety to
ensure the right foundation

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:56.430
for analytics and AI.

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:03.330
In the transformational
phase, your organization

00:14:03.330 --> 00:14:05.730
is actively working to
develop the technology

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:09.330
and processes to allow data
scientists to create, share,

00:14:09.330 --> 00:14:11.940
discover, and reuse data
and machine-learning

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:15.150
assets across different
teams and functions.

00:14:15.150 --> 00:14:18.960
Moreover, standardizing the
definition, storage, and access

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:20.670
of machine learning
data sets, you

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:23.393
invest in implementing
a feature store.

00:14:23.393 --> 00:14:25.310
A feature store can be
a federated [INAUDIBLE]

00:14:25.310 --> 00:14:27.930
repository for
registering new features

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:32.880
and discovering existing ones
to be used by data scientists.

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:34.350
Now we move to the secure theme.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:37.650
A secure theme concerns
with protecting your data,

00:14:37.650 --> 00:14:39.870
securing your
machine-learning services,

00:14:39.870 --> 00:14:41.850
and ensuring responsible AI.

00:14:44.750 --> 00:14:47.900
As a tactical step to enable
AI adoption with confidence,

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:51.140
your organization defines the
identity and access-management

00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:55.010
policies and security controls
to protect your data and AI

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:56.210
services.

00:14:56.210 --> 00:14:58.430
In addition, you
ensure data privacy

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:01.820
through constant sensitive-data
classification and obfuscation.

00:15:05.790 --> 00:15:07.800
In the strategic phase,
your organization

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:10.740
starts to implement a
comprehensive data-governance

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:14.790
program covering data-access
auditing, lineage tracking,

00:15:14.790 --> 00:15:18.510
data privacy and compliance,
and establishing responsible AI

00:15:18.510 --> 00:15:20.250
practices.

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:22.740
Responsible AI practices
ensure building

00:15:22.740 --> 00:15:25.110
fair and explainable
AI solutions

00:15:25.110 --> 00:15:27.300
to maintain the
desired level of trust

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:29.850
in AI throughout your
business functions.

00:15:29.850 --> 00:15:32.640
For more information, we
recommend watching the session

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:34.020
on Responsible AI--

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:36.210
From Theory to
Practice by Tracy Frey.

00:15:40.520 --> 00:15:42.800
In the transformational
phase, your data governance

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:46.700
is streamlined using automated
workflows to radically validate

00:15:46.700 --> 00:15:50.060
new use cases against the
domain regulations and your AI

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:51.110
principles.

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:53.480
In addition, you
invest in AI safety

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:55.907
and robustness to
improve the reliability

00:15:55.907 --> 00:15:58.115
and generalizability of your
machine-learning models.

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:03.460
The scale theme covers
using cloud-native services

00:16:03.460 --> 00:16:07.090
and accelerators to scale your
machine-learning workflows.

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:08.890
In the tactical phase,
your organization

00:16:08.890 --> 00:16:11.260
aimed at controlling the
cost of experimenting

00:16:11.260 --> 00:16:12.460
with machine learning.

00:16:12.460 --> 00:16:15.310
Thus, you usually
dedicate cloud resources

00:16:15.310 --> 00:16:18.550
with limited compute power for
a few data scientists who work

00:16:18.550 --> 00:16:20.980
with small, offline data sets.

00:16:20.980 --> 00:16:23.950
At the strategic phase, data
ingest and transformation

00:16:23.950 --> 00:16:26.530
are performed using
managed processing services

00:16:26.530 --> 00:16:28.370
like Dataflow and Dataproc.

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:32.320
They execute large-scale
batch and streaming ETL jobs.

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:34.670
Similarly,
machine-learning training

00:16:34.670 --> 00:16:36.550
and batched scoring
jobs are performed

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:38.800
using cloud-managed services.

00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:41.890
This enable running powerful
machine-learning algorithms

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:47.870
on large data sets at scale
with no infrastructure overhead.

00:16:47.870 --> 00:16:50.700
For example, we work with
a digital-native customer

00:16:50.700 --> 00:16:53.150
who used to run their
machine-learning workflows

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:54.710
on dedicated VMs.

00:16:54.710 --> 00:16:58.570
However, by moving to the AI
platform which provides managed

00:16:58.570 --> 00:17:01.520
services to train and deploy
machine-learning models,

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:04.250
the customer now is able
to scale their training

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:07.338
and scoring jobs to more
markets as well as to reduce

00:17:07.338 --> 00:17:08.630
the cost of running these jobs.

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:13.980
As you moves to the
transformational phase,

00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:17.190
you invest in establishing
a unified and integrated

00:17:17.190 --> 00:17:19.290
machine-learning
platform which helps

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:21.839
to streamline the transition
from experimentation

00:17:21.839 --> 00:17:24.630
to production and to
serve all data scientists

00:17:24.630 --> 00:17:27.450
and machine-learning
engineers and different teams.

00:17:27.450 --> 00:17:29.670
This integrated
platform provides access

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:32.730
to standardized tools,
frameworks, templates,

00:17:32.730 --> 00:17:35.490
services, accelerators,
and processes

00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:39.120
for the entire organization.

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:41.790
Finally, we cover
the ultimate theme,

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:44.430
which concerns with
deploying, executing,

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:49.510
and operating machine-learning
workloads in production.

00:17:49.510 --> 00:17:52.540
In the technical phase, the
process to build AI systems

00:17:52.540 --> 00:17:55.700
is usually manual every
step, from data analysis

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:58.960
to preparation to model
training and deployment.

00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:01.060
Such a manual process
prevents the organization

00:18:01.060 --> 00:18:03.460
from scaling the number
of models they use

00:18:03.460 --> 00:18:05.305
and the frequency of
updating these models.

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:11.070
As your organization moves
to the strategic phase,

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:13.650
you automate data processing
and analytics pipelines

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:16.110
to be executed on
recurrent schedules

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:19.500
or to tackle critical
events and triggers.

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:22.710
At this stage, you deploy
end-to-end continuous training

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:25.590
pipelines to regularly update
your machine-learning models

00:18:25.590 --> 00:18:27.000
with the new data.

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:29.430
This enables your
model to rapidly adapt

00:18:29.430 --> 00:18:32.560
to the changes in the
dynamics of your business.

00:18:32.560 --> 00:18:35.440
For example, we're currently
working with a telecom company

00:18:35.440 --> 00:18:38.860
to automate retraining their
propensity models using

00:18:38.860 --> 00:18:41.860
TFX and Kubeflow pipelines,
allowing the models to be

00:18:41.860 --> 00:18:44.710
updated weekly instead
of updating them manually

00:18:44.710 --> 00:18:46.120
each six or eight weeks.

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:51.570
In the transformational
phase, your goal

00:18:51.570 --> 00:18:53.970
is to develop a machine-learning
engineering culture

00:18:53.970 --> 00:18:57.030
and practice that unifies
both machine-learning system

00:18:57.030 --> 00:18:59.920
development and machine-learning
system operations.

00:18:59.920 --> 00:19:01.850
We call that MLOps.

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:04.830
MLOps strongly advocates
automation and monitoring

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:08.010
at all steps of machine-learning
system construction.

00:19:08.010 --> 00:19:09.990
With this approach,
you are looking

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:13.650
towards a shorter deployment
cycles, increased deployment

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:17.330
velocity, and faster
time to market.

00:19:17.330 --> 00:19:19.560
This, however, requires
robust quality control

00:19:19.560 --> 00:19:22.280
throughout the machine-learning
training and deployment phases

00:19:22.280 --> 00:19:25.690
as well as continuous training
and continuous monitoring

00:19:25.690 --> 00:19:28.310
of your model's
performance in production.

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:31.200
Back to Donna to conclude.

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:33.300
DONNA SCHUT: Thank you, Khalid.

00:19:33.300 --> 00:19:37.380
To summarize, the three key
points of our framework are,

00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:41.340
one, anyone can
use this framework.

00:19:41.340 --> 00:19:43.020
No matter where
you're starting, you

00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:45.990
can use this framework
to define your strategy

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:48.840
and drive successful adoption.

00:19:48.840 --> 00:19:52.770
Two, success requires
an integrated lens.

00:19:52.770 --> 00:19:55.470
In order to build an
effective AI capability,

00:19:55.470 --> 00:19:58.020
you need to address six themes--

00:19:58.020 --> 00:20:03.980
learn, lead, access,
secure, scale, and automate.

00:20:03.980 --> 00:20:07.030
And three, there is value
every step of the way.

00:20:07.030 --> 00:20:09.000
It's not about becoming
transformational

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:10.410
in every aspect.

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:14.940
It's about gaining
value in each phase.

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:17.010
So what can you do next?

00:20:17.010 --> 00:20:18.590
You can create a
group of leaders

00:20:18.590 --> 00:20:21.920
who will be responsible
for your AI strategy.

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:23.510
And from there,
each of you should

00:20:23.510 --> 00:20:25.550
use this framework
to identify where

00:20:25.550 --> 00:20:27.830
you are in your AI journey.

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:30.230
Then collectively set your goal.

00:20:30.230 --> 00:20:33.920
Where do you envision
your organization going?

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:35.900
Based on the gaps,
establish a plan

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:38.750
for evolving your AI capability.

00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:41.600
We are here to help you
every step of the way.

00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:44.150
Check out our resources
and read our white paper

00:20:44.150 --> 00:20:46.080
for more information.

00:20:46.080 --> 00:20:49.030
Thank you for
watching this session.

